  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">o-Nitrophenol is insoluble in sodium hydrogen carbonate because it is less acidic than carbonic acid.While, others being more acidic than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;dissolve in sodium bi&nbsp;carbonate.</p><p>&nbsp;Hence, the given&nbsp;reaction will not be spontaneous.&nbsp;<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/EM0026256DUP02HIN1.JPG\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 98px;\" /></p>",
